      "evidence": "The override regex is anchored to bare test basenames, but the focused nextest log identifies the tests by full names such as runtime_v2::tests::unified_runtime_kernel::runtime_v2_unified_runtime_kernel_events_are_correlated. Under nextest test-filter semantics, the anchored basename regex therefore does not match those full test names. The focused validator uses a different, unanchored substring expression and completes in about 5 seconds, so it neither demonstrates that the override selects the three tests nor that the 240s setting is applied. Consequently, the SOR claim that the hosted timeout was stabilized is not yet supported.",
      "recommendation": "Use an exact regex over the three fully qualified nextest test names, optionally constrained to the adl binary/package, and add validation using the same selector to prove that exactly those three tests match. Keep the 240s terminate-after=1 setting and the profile-wide 120s default unchanged, then leave full hosted workspace coverage as the fail-closed integration proof."
    }
  ],
  "residual_risks": [
    "The focused local run is much faster than the hosted coverage failure and cannot reproduce hosted contention or prove the extended ceiling is sufficient.",
    "Full hosted workspace coverage remains pending and must pass before integration or merge.",
    "No Runtime v2 product or test source files appear in the scoped change, so semantic/assertion drift is not indicated by the supplied diff."
  ],
  "one_sentence_summary": "The change is bounded in intent and contains no product-semantic edits, but the anchored nextest filter appears not to match the fully qualified test names, making the shared-gate fix ineffective until corrected and selector-matched validation is recorded."
